==English==

===Etymology===
From {{term|telephone}}

Telephony is a [[portmanteau]] word derived from the French word téléphone, a combination of ancient Greek τῆλε (tēle), “‘afar’”) + φωνή (phōnē), “‘voice, sound’”)

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/təˈlɛf.ə.ni/}}, {{SAMPA|/t@"lEf.@.ni/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-}}

# The act of [[sound]] transmission via the [[electromagnetic]] [[spectrum]].
# The study and application of telephone technology.

